<title>USA: Archer critical of U.S. tax simplification plan.</title>
<headline>Archer critical of U.S. tax simplification plan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>House Ways and Means Chairman Bill Archer, R-Texas, criticized the administration's tax simplication plan Monday, saying it would add $6.1 billion in taxes.</p>
<p>&quot;The tax code can and should be simplified, but we can do so without raising taxes,&quot; Archer said in a statement.</p>
<p>He urged the administration to drop tax hikes from the budget proposal, pay for any tax simplifications only with spending cuts and submit a proposal that fundamentally changes the tax code.</p>
</text>
